  "slug": "coherent-unitary-6215",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend programmable unitary photonic hardware to optical neural networks, modular tiling, and spectral measurement.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is programmable unitary interferometric circuits as the computational primitive for coherent photonic systems. Two preprints address unitary transformations directly: one proposes a logarithmic-depth butterfly interferometer architecture for parameter-efficient unitary transformations in coherent optical neural networks, and the other proposes a modular processor built from unitary tiles of fixed mixers and programmable phases, evaluated by numerical fitting. A third preprint applies the same kind of hardware differently, realizing a universal silicon photonic chip in which unequal path lengths between two 8x8 unitary circuits enable simultaneous spectral measurement and programmable filtering at 0.05 nm resolution. What is new is the joint emphasis on depth-efficient parameterization, modular tiling of unitary elements, and multifunctional use across computation and measurement.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
